      sources: "Sources: Learn, Entra CBA Certificate Revocation List; Graph national cloud deployments; Entra feature availability. Chapter 05, “Which cloud, for this check.”",
      say: `Which cloud you're in changes the answer. For interactive sign-in, a CRL must stay under twenty megabytes in public Entra ID, which includes GCC, and forty-five in Azure US Government, which includes GCC High. Either way it must download within ten seconds. So the expected-configuration file holds both sets, and the check takes a cloud name with no default. Learn doesn't say which megabyte it means, so the configuration reads the decimal one, the stricter reading.`,
      detail: `Learn gives two sets of CRL limits. For interactive sign-in, a CRL must stay under 20 MB in public Entra ID, which includes GCC, and 45 MB in Azure US Government, which Learn's FAQ says includes GCC High and L5; it must download within 10 seconds. The service-side limits are 65 MB and 150 MB. config/cba-expected.json holds both sets per cloud name, and the check takes --cloud gcc, gcchigh or dod with no default. Learn writes the limits in MB without saying whether a megabyte is 1,000,000 or 1,048,576 bytes; the configuration reads them as decimal, the stricter reading. The Graph reads go to graph.microsoft.com for GCC and graph.microsoft.us or dod-graph.microsoft.us for GCC High and L5. Certificate-based authentication and Conditional Access are available in Azure for US Government.`,
