      sources: "Sources: Learn, CBA CRL; x509CertificateRule; authentication strengths; BOD 25-01 required configurations. Chapter 05, “The check.”",
      say: `Here are the thirteen rules, each labeled with its source. Most come straight from Learn: a CA with no CRL, an endpoint that isn't HTTP, a CRL over the size limit or slower than ten seconds, the certificate method switched off, and CRL validation off or a CA exempted. Some are the program's own design: an early warning at eighty percent, a CRL nobody measured, a CA expiring within ninety days, and an issuing CA missing from the trust store. And two protect the strength: PIV mapped to multifactor, and an enforced phishing-resistant policy.`,
      detail: `CB-01 Finding; Warn: an intermediate CA with no CRL configured (Finding); a root CA with none (Warn); Learn: no CRL, no revocation check. CB-02 Warn: a CRL endpoint that isn't HTTP; Learn recommends HTTP. CB-03 Finding: a CRL over the cloud's interactive size limit; Learn. CB-04 Finding: a CRL that couldn't be downloaded, or took more than 10 seconds; Learn. CB-05 Warn: a CRL over 80% of the limit; design guidance (warnPercent). CB-06 Finding: a configured CRL with no measurement; design guidance: measure every CRL. CB-07 Finding: the X.509 certificate method isn't enabled; Learn. CB-08 Warn: CRL validation isn't enabled, or a CA is exempted; Learn recommends enforcing it and exempting only to troubleshoot. CB-09 Finding: a PIV policy OID not mapped to multifactor, with a single-factor default; Learn's mode rules; the program's OIDs. CB-10 Finding: no enabled policy for all users and resources requires a phishing-resistant strength; SCuBA MS.AAD.3.1v1; Learn's strengths. CB-11 Warn: a CA certificate that expires within 90 days; design guidance (caExpiryWarnDays). CB-12 Finding: an issuing CA the card program uses isn't in the trust store; design guidance. CB-13 Warn: a low-affinity binding field (PrincipalName, RFC822Name) configured; the validation kit's affinity table; ADM Gate 6's decision.`,
