      sources: "Sources: Learn, CBA CRL; PKI and CA lists; certificateAuthorityDetail; x509 method, rule, binding; strengths; CA policies; feature availability. Chapter 05, “Verified facts.”",
      say: `The verified facts, all read on November first. The CRL limits are generally available: twenty and forty-five megabytes for interactive sign-in, a ten-second download, and larger service limits. Entra checks CRLs up to ten CAs toward the root. The trust store, the certificate method, the strengths and the Conditional Access policies are all in Graph version one point oh, with the permissions you just saw. The certificate method's bindings include the low-affinity principal name and email fields. And both features are available in Azure for US Government.`,
      detail: `CRL limits: interactive 20 MB (public, includes GCC) and 45 MB (Azure US Government, includes GCC High and L5); 10-second download; service limits 65 MB and 150 MB; applies in US Government clouds with the larger limits; GA. CRL behavior: no CRL, no revocation check; one endpoint, HTTP or HTTPS, HTTP recommended; a configured CRL that can't be downloaded fails CBA; CRLs checked up to 10 CAs toward the root; GA. List certificateBasedAuthPki; list its certificateAuthorities: PublicKeyInfrastructure.Read.All; Authentication Administrator or Privileged Authentication Administrator; L4 and L5; v1.0. certificateAuthorityDetail: certificateRevocationListUrl, certificateAuthorityType, thumbprint, expirationDateTime, issuerSubjectKeyIdentifier; v1.0. Get X.509 certificate method: Policy.Read.AuthenticationMethod; Global Reader or Authentication Policy Administrator; L4 and L5 (not 21Vianet); v1.0. X.509 method properties: authenticationModeConfiguration (rules by issuerSubject or policyOID), crlValidationConfiguration, certificateUserBindings (PrincipalName, RFC822Name, SubjectKeyIdentifier, SHA1PublicKey); v1.0. List authentication strength policies: Policy.Read.AuthenticationMethod; allowedCombinations from authenticationMethodModes; L4 and L5; v1.0. List Conditional Access policies: Policy.Read.All; v1.0. Legacy certificateBasedAuthConfiguration: Organization.Read.All; Global Administrator is the only delegated role; L4 and L5; v1.0. CBA and Conditional Access: available in Azure for US Government; GA.`,
