      say: `Lab 2 uses a test tenant with certificate-based authentication set up for a test CA; the authors haven't run it. Register a reader app with a certificate and only the three permissions. Export the configuration and check its shape matches the fixture. Measure the real CRLs from outside the agency network. Run the check with your test PKI's thumbprints and policy OIDs, and your cloud. Then the real proof: revoke a test certificate, wait for the next CRL, and sign in. Entra should refuse it. Finally, back everything out.`,
      detail: `Not run by the authors. Use a test tenant with certificate-based authentication configured for a test CA, never production. Work in examples/hr-lifecycle. 1 Register the reader app with a certificate, and grant the three application permissions from Lab 1, step 1, with admin consent, and nothing else. 2 Export the configuration: with a token for the reader app in HRLC_GRAPH_TOKEN, list the PKI containers (GET https://graph.microsoft.com/v1.0/directory/publicKeyInfrastructure/certificateBasedAuthConfigurations), then python python/graph_export.py --task cba-read --cloud gcc --param pkiId=<pki-id> --out exports/cba. Check that x509-method.json holds one object and that each CA in pki-cas.json carries certificateRevocationListUrl as the fixture does. 3 Measure the real CRLs: put each CA's CRL URL in a file, one per line, and run measure from outside the agency network; record the run's date with the file. 4 Check: copy config/cba-expected.json with the CA thumbprints and PIV policy OIDs replaced by the test PKI's, and run check with --cloud set to the test tenant's cloud. 5 Prove revocation: revoke a test user's certificate, wait for the CA's next CRL publication, and sign in with it. Entra should refuse it with the revoked-certificate error Learn lists. Record the revocation time, the CRL's publication time and the refused sign-in. 6 Back it out: remove the permissions, delete the reader app and its certificate, and reissue the test user's certificate if you need it again. Then delete exports and out, with the lab's two files.`,
